for (const [initializerIdentifier, componentIdentifiers] of Object.entries(jsComponentInitializers)) {
  const initializerFunc = DotNet.findJSFunction(initializerIdentifier, 0) as JSComponentInitializerCallback;
  for (const componentIdentifier of componentIdentifiers)
    initializerFunc(componentIdentifier, jsComponentParameters[componentIdentifier]);
}

if (manager && currentRendererId === rendererId) {
    // A different renderer type (e.g., Server vs WebAssembly) is trying to enable JS root components.
    // This is a multi-host scenario which is not supported for dynamic root components.
    throw new Error('Dynamic root components have already been enabled.');
  }

// When the same renderer type re-enables (e.g., circuit restart or new circuit on same page),
  // accept the new manager. The old manager's DotNetObjectReference is no longer valid anyway
  // because the old circuit is gone. We don't dispose the old manager - doing so would cause
  // JSDisconnectedException because the circuit that created it no longer exists.
  currentRendererId = rendererId;
  manager = managerInstance;

[Theory]
[InlineData("ServerNonPrerendered")]
[InlineData("WebAssemblyNonPrerendered")]
public void PersistentStateIsSupportedInDynamicJSRoots(string renderMode)
{
    Navigate($"subdir/WasmMinimal/dynamic-js-root.html?renderMode={renderMode}");

    Browser.Equal("Counter", () => Browser.Exists(By.TagName("h1")).Text);
    Browser.Equal("Current count: 0", () => Browser.Exists(By.CssSelector("p[role='status']")).Text);

    Browser.Click(By.CssSelector("button.btn-primary"));
    Browser.Equal("Current count: 1", () => Browser.Exists(By.CssSelector("p[role='status']")).Text);
}

findings.body:
The guard at line 126 throws only when `currentRendererId === rendererId`. That is the same-renderer restart the PR is meant to allow, so a second circuit on the same page fails with "Dynamic root components have already been enabled." The comment and PR description say the opposite. A different renderer type (Server vs WebAssembly, IDs 1 and 2 in `WebRendererId.cs`) should throw, but this condition lets it through and silently replaces `manager`.

::diff{file="src/Components/Web.JS/src/Rendering/JSRootComponents.ts" lines="120-137"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The condition needs `!==`. Once it is flipped, the cross-host case throws as the description requires.

As written, the first circuit is fine because `manager` is undefined, so the existing E2E test still passes. A real restart on the same page would throw.

The moved `PersistentStateIsSupportedInDynamicJSRoots` theory loads the page once and clicks a button. That is the first-enable path, where `manager` is undefined, so the guard never runs.

::code{file="src/Components/test/E2ETest/Tests/StatePersistenceTest.cs" lines="279-291"}

The description's two scenarios each need their own test: (1) a second circuit on the same page must enable and `Blazor.rootComponents.add` must succeed, and (2) a Server plus WebAssembly host on one page must throw. Neither is covered, and the inverted guard and the missing parameter assignment both pass this test. Note that the test does not assert that `add()` resolves, only that the rendered text changes.

Before the PR, the `dynamic-js-root-counter` registration applied only when the `RegisterDynamicJSRootComponent` flag was passed, through a dedicated test-server site. The PR removes that gate and the dedicated site, so `RazorComponentEndpointsStartup` now registers a JS root for every app built on it.

::diff{file="src/Components/test/testassets/Components.TestServer/RazorComponentEndpointsStartup.cs" lines="51-56"}

Since `attachWebRendererInterop` only calls `enableJSRootComponents` when the parameter map is non-empty, every Razor endpoints E2E test now runs the dynamic JS root code path. That changes the baseline for unrelated tests, and it means the bug in the previous finding would also affect them. The grep found no remaining references to the removed `Razor Component Endpoints with JS Root Component` site, so nothing dangles. The cost is blast radius, not a broken reference.
